#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# ordering

#% text
# `ordering(xs)` gives the positions of the elements of `xs` in sorted order; `ordering(xs, n)` the first `n` (the last `-n` for negative `n`).

#% text
# `ordering(xs, n, p)` orders by the predicate `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `xs[ordering(xs)]` is `sort(xs)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
ordering([c, a, b])
#% output
#= [2, 3, 1]

#% cell
ordering([3, 1, 2], 2)
#% output
#= [2, 3]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# By a predicate:

#% cell
ordering([3, 1, 2], all, greater)
#% output
#= [1, 3, 2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sort`, `sort_by`
